CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*sdevice->hostdata)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct storvsc_dev_hostdata)...)
#94: FILE: drivers/scsi/storvsc_drv.c:1444:
+	sdevice->hostdata = kzalloc(sizeof(struct storvsc_dev_hostdata),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

